From c4f2f2186d687c29e9086ea0c90424f1e22c06e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:29:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] vmlinux link fixes: weak typeof externs, strcmp literal
 folding, symbol-diff immediates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five root causes stood between vmlinux.o and a linked kernel image; the
first two are C-frontend gaps, the rest x86 assembler gaps. All are
proven against GCC/GAS output.

1) Block-scope `extern typeof(f) f __attribute__((weak, visibility
   ("hidden")))` dropped both attributes: typeof supplies the function
   type, `derived` stays empty, so the declaration bypassed the
   function-decl handler that propagates symbol attrs. The kernel's
   !CONFIG_MODULES symbol_get() (module.h:835) expands to exactly this
   shape; ips_link_to_i915_driver stayed a GLOBAL undef and vmlinux
   failed to link instead of weak-resolving to NULL.
   lower_extern_decl now pushes weak/visibility for every named extern.
   PROOF: wk4.c readelf shows `WEAK HIDDEN UND` — identical to GCC.

2) __builtin_strcmp/strncmp/memcmp on two string literals now fold at
   lowering time (value = sign of first differing byte; strncmp/memcmp
   only with a constant length). GCC folds these at -O0; the kernel's
   vruntime_cmp (CachyMod fair.c) depends on it — the unmatched-operator
   branch calls the deliberately undefined __BUILD_BUG_vruntime_cmp,
   which must be eliminated as dead code. fair.o previously kept the
   call and vmlinux failed with "undefined reference to
   `__BUILD_BUG_vruntime_cmp'".
   PROOF: regression builtin_strcmp_fold.c (kernel macro idiom + runtime
   semantics vs glibc); fair.o has no BUILD_BUG relocs after the fix.

3) `$identity_mapped - 0b` immediates (relocate_kernel_64.S): the
   label-diff scanner did not trim around '-', so the whole expression
   fell through to a PLAIN SYMBOL named "identity_mapped - 0b" → ld
   "undefined reference". Now parsed as SymbolDiff.

4) SymbolDiff immediates were unsupported by the ALU encoder. New arm
   emits the 0x81 imm32 form and records a diff relocation; resolution
   in resolve_internal_relocations understands NUMERIC local labels
   (`0b`) on either side, folds same-section pairs to constants, and
   converts extern-minus-local to R_X86_64_PC32 with the addend
   adjusted by the label position (S - addr(0b)) — the exact reloc GAS
   emits for this shape.
   PROOF: asm-diff imm_symbol_diff.s byte-identical; relk2.s reloc
   `ext_fwd + 3` matches GAS.

5) `$(srso_safe_ret)+5` (nospec-branch.h __HANDLE_INTR_SAFERET):
   parenthesized symbols in symbol+offset immediates were rejected and
   degenerated to a literal-string reloc "(srso_safe_ret)+5". Parens now
   strip to the bare symbol; addend preserved.
   PROOF: srso.s relocs `ext_sym + 5` / `ext_sym + 0` identical to GAS.

Deviation note (documented in the encoder): backward-defined
same-section diffs fold to imm8 in GAS at parse time; lccc emits the
semantically identical imm32. The kernel's uses are all forward
references where GAS also reserves imm32.

Validation: cargo test 685 pass; regression 191 pass (+1 new);
correctness 50/50; intrinsics 3/3; linker 86/86; asm-diff ALL RAW .text
BYTES EXACT (+1 new case).
