From d2c2f9ffc89a63891f13a07fe73bed9caad66cad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] x86/i686 asm: ljmpl with symbol-difference offset
 (la57toggle.S)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`ljmpl $__KERNEL_CS, $(.Lret - trampoline_32bit_src)` — the direct far
jump in the LA57 trampoline carries a same-section label difference as
its offset immediate. Both encoders (x86-64 encode_ljmp and the i686
one that handles .code32 inside 64-bit kernel objects) only accepted
Integer/Symbol offsets and rejected the file with "ljmp requires
$segment, $offset operands", stopping the kernel build at
arch/x86/boot/startup/la57toggle.o.

New arm: emit 0xEA, record a diff relocation on the imm32 field, append
the segment word. Same-section pairs fold to a constant after layout via
the existing diff-reloc resolution.

PROOF: lj.s (.code32 + ljmpl label-diff) — .rodata bytes
`90 ea 08000000 1000 90` identical to GAS. la57toggle.o now assembles.

Validation: full battery green (685 lib / 191 regression / 50
correctness / 3 intrinsics / 86 linker / asm-diff RAW EXACT).
