From e2b78abc334031f81ed38a960eb27994e598dafd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Boot-path assembler: displacement diffs, .irpc, jmpl,
 multi-symbol .globl, mov/ljmp diff immediates, 16-bit symbol movs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Continuing the bzImage blocker chain after vmlinux.o linked. Every fix is
byte-verified against GAS output.

1) Displacement::SymbolDiff/SymbolDiffAddend: head_64.S's rva() macro
   produces `((gdt) - startup_32)(%ebp)` and `((pgtable + 0) -
   startup_32)(%ebp)` — label differences (optionally with constant
   addend) as memory displacements. New parser arms + both encoders
   (x86-64/i686) thread a diff relocation through encode_modrm_mem;
   same-section pairs fold to constants after layout (no reloc emitted,
   byte-identical: lea2.s/lea3.s vs GAS).
   RIP-relative + SymbolDiff is rejected loudly (meaningless).

2) numeric_labels.rs resolve_numeric_displacement lacked SymbolDiff arms:
   `leal (_bss - 1b)(%ecx), %edi` (efi-mixed.S) left the raw "1b" name
   in the reloc. Now either side resolves; extern-minus-local converts to
   R_X86_64_PC32 with addend = P - addr(label) — identical to GAS
   (efm4.s: `_bss + 4` PC32).

3) .irpc (character iteration) implemented in the GAS macro expander,
   and the .rept pre-pass now tracks .irpc blocks so their .endr is not
   swallowed (previously the body leaked one stray instruction per
   iteration). efi-mixed.S `.irpc l, 0123` page-table unroll is
   byte-identical (irpc.s).

4) i686: `jmpl` mnemonic aliased to jmp (pmjump.S `jmpl *%eax` = ff e0);
   `mov $sym_diff, %reg` (head_64.S `movl $(_bss - startup_32), %ecx`);
   16-bit `movw $sym, %reg` emits B8+rd iw with R_386_16 (header.S
   realmode `movw $_end, %dx`); `test $imm, LABEL` routes the bare-label
   operand through the absolute-memory path (header.S
   `testb $CAN_USE_HEAP, loadflags`).

5) x86-64: mov $sym_diff imm32 (B8+rd id + folded diff), ljmpl
   $seg, $(a - b) far-jump offsets in both encoders
   (la57toggle.S trampoline: `ea 08000000 1000` == GAS).

6) `.globl a, b` (comma list) marks EVERY name global. mkpiggy emits
   `.globl input_data, input_data_end`; the single-string handling left
   both LOCAL and the compressed vmlinux link failed with "hidden symbol
   `input_data' isn't defined".

7) Kernel tree fix (not lccc): R8169 Kconfig now selects PAGE_POOL —
   the 1020-r8169 multi-queue patch uses page_pool_* but never selected
   it; link failed identically under GCC. (Reported for upstreaming to
   the CachyMod patch; kept local to the kernel tree.)

Validation: 685 lib / 191 regression / 50 correctness / 86 linker green;
asm-diff ALL RAW .text BYTES EXACT.

Known remaining gap (next commit): true .code16 encoding — the i686
encoder emits 32-bit ModR/M inside .code16 (GAS uses 16-bit addressing
modes + R_*_16 relocs there). Affects arch/x86/boot/header.o.
